.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt WPA_SUPPLICANT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wpa_supplicant
.Nd join and keep a Wi-Fi network
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl BdhKLqtvWy
.Op Fl D Ar driver
.Op Fl P Ar pidfile
.Op Fl f Ar logfile
.Op Fl g Ar global_ctrl
.Op Fl G Ar group
.Fl i Ar ifname
.Fl c Ar config
.Op Fl C Ar ctrl
.Op Fl p Ar driver_param
.Op Fl I Ar config
.Op Fl N Fl i Ar ifname Fl c Ar config ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is hostap's Wi-Fi station, version 2.12.
It reads the networks of
.Ar config ,
described in
.Xr wpa_supplicant.conf 5 ,
scans for them on the interface
.Ar ifname ,
chooses one, associates with it and authenticates, and keeps the link:
it joins again when the access point drops it and, with
.Cm bgscan ,
moves to a stronger access point of the same network.
It speaks to the radio through the kernel's nl80211 interface and sends
the authentication frames of 802.1X and the four-way handshake as EAPOL
packets.
.Pp
Rach2 builds it statically with OpenSSL.
It joins open networks and those of WPA (TKIP), WPA2 (CCMP) and WPA3-Personal
(SAE, with management-frame protection), with a passphrase or with
WPA2-Enterprise's 802.1X using EAP-PEAP, EAP-TTLS or EAP-TLS, and MSCHAPv2,
GTC or MD5 inside the tunnel.
WPS, Wi-Fi Direct, the access-point and mesh modes, DPP, OWE, Hotspot 2.0
and D-Bus are not built.
.Pp
While it runs,
.Xr wpa_cli 8
controls it through the control interface that
.Cm ctrl_interface
names in
.Ar config .
Run with
.Fl c
and neither an interface nor a control interface,
.Nm
reads
.Ar config ,
reports what it finds wrong and exits.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl B
Run in the background once the interfaces are set up.
.It Fl c Ar config
Read the networks and settings of the interface from
.Ar config .
.It Fl C Ar ctrl
The control interface's directory, when no
.Fl c
gives one.
.It Fl d
Print more of what happens; given twice, more still.
.It Fl D Ar driver
The driver interface;
.Cm nl80211 ,
the default, is the only one built.
.It Fl f Ar logfile
Append the messages to
.Ar logfile
instead of the standard output.
.It Fl g Ar global_ctrl
Open a global control interface at the path
.Ar global_ctrl ,
through which interfaces are added and removed while it runs.
.It Fl G Ar group
The group that owns the global control interface.
.It Fl h
Print the usage and exit.
.It Fl i Ar ifname
The wireless interface to manage.
.It Fl I Ar config
A second configuration file, read after
.Fl c .
.It Fl K
Print keys and passwords in the messages.
.It Fl L
Print the license and exit.
.It Fl N
Begin the options of a further interface.
.It Fl p Ar driver_param
Parameters for the driver interface.
.It Fl P Ar pidfile
Write the process number to
.Ar pidfile .
.It Fl q
Print less; given twice, less still.
.It Fl t
Begin each message with the time.
.It Fl v
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl W
Wait for a monitor to attach to the control interface before starting.
.It Fl y
Print the details of parsing the configuration.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/run/wpa_supplicant/ Ns Ar ifname
The control interface's socket, when the configuration sets
.Cm ctrl_interface
to
.Pa /var/run/wpa_supplicant .
.It Pa /etc/hostap.COPYING , /etc/openssl.LICENSE , /etc/libnl.COPYING
The licenses of hostap and of the libraries it links.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Join a WPA2 network whose passphrase is in the configuration, then show
the link:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
wpa_passphrase home 'a long passphrase' > /etc/wlan0.conf
wpa_supplicant -B -i wlan0 -c /etc/wlan0.conf
wpa_cli -i wlan0 status
.Ed
.Pp
Check a configuration file:
.Dl wpa_supplicant -c /etc/wlan0.conf
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr wpa_supplicant.conf 5 ,
.Xr hostapd 8 ,
.Xr iw 8 ,
.Xr rfkill 8 ,
.Xr wpa_cli 8 ,
.Xr wpa_passphrase 8
.Sh STANDARDS
IEEE 802.11-2020 and IEEE 802.1X-2020.
